# Git commits

## Enforcement (strict)

- This rule is **mandatory** for all agent-authored git actions in this repository.
- If a git command would violate any section below, **do not run it**. Stop, explain the exact rule conflict, and ask for explicit user confirmation or clarification.
- When multiple instructions exist, prefer the **most restrictive** interpretation that keeps history safe and intentional.

## When commits are allowed

- **Create a git commit only when the user explicitly asks** (e.g. "commit this", "make a commit", "git commit"). Phrases like "save my work" or "checkpoint" count as explicit only if they clearly mean a **git commit**—when in doubt, **ask** before committing.
- **Do not commit** to "helpfully" save progress, to finish a task, or because a change set "feels done." **Never** run `git commit` without a clear, direct request to commit.
- **Do not** amend, rebase, or otherwise rewrite history unless the user explicitly asks.

## Push and branches

- **Do not** `git push` (or force-push) unless the user **explicitly** asks to push.
- **Do not** merge or rebase branches unless the user **explicitly** asks (same spirit as commits).

### Branch model (this project)

| Branch | Role |
|--------|------|
| **`master`** | **Root / release line.** Stable, production-ready history. Does **not** receive direct feature work. Updates from **`dev`** follow the **`dev` -> `master`** subsection below (compatibility + pull request). |
| **`dev`** | **Integration branch.** Collects completed work from **feature** branches. Merge feature branches into `dev` only after **checking compatibility** with current `dev` (build runs, conflicts resolved, smoke test as the user defines). |
| **`feature/<name>`** | **Feature development.** One branch per feature or task slice (e.g. `feature/usgs-connector`, `feature/globe-heatmap`). Open from up-to-date **`dev`**, implement, then merge into **`dev`** when ready—not directly into `master`. |

**Intended flow:** `feature/...` -> **`dev`** (integrate & verify) -> **`master`** (release). Hotfixes from `master` are **out of scope** unless the user explicitly asks.

### `dev` -> `master` (release only when compatible + pull request)

- **`dev` may be merged into `master` only when both are true:** (1) **`dev` is compatible**—build succeeds, conflicts resolved, and any checks the user cares about (tests, CI, smoke paths) have been satisfied; (2) the integration happens through a **pull request** (`dev` -> `master`) on the hosting platform, reviewed and merged there—not as an informal local-only merge by default.
- **Agent behavior:** Do **not** run or recommend `git checkout master && git merge dev` as the **normal** release path. Tell the user to **open and complete a PR** from `dev` into `master` after compatibility is confirmed. A **local** merge is acceptable **only** if the user **explicitly** asks **and** states the **PR has already been merged** on the remote, **or** that they waive PR for this repo and confirm **compatibility**—when in doubt, **ask**.
- **No remote / no PR host:** `dev` -> `master` still requires an **explicit user request** plus **stated compatibility**; never merge silently.

**Agent defaults when the user asks for a new branch:** create **`feature/<short-descriptive-slug>`** from **`dev`** unless the user specifies another name or base.

## Staging scope

- **Stage only** paths the user named, or changes that clearly belong to the requested commit. If the working tree has **other** modified or untracked files, **list them** and either leave them unstaged or **ask**—**do not** silently `git add -A` unless the user explicitly asked to commit **everything**.
- Before committing, prefer **`git status`** so staged vs unstaged is intentional.

## One logical change per commit

- Prefer **one coherent story** per commit. If the working tree mixes unrelated changes, **tell the user** and offer **split commits** or **ask** which single prefix and scope they want.

## Safety (never commit)

- **Secrets:** Do not commit API keys, passwords, tokens, private keys, or full `.env` files. If such material appears staged, **stop**, warn, and remove it from the index before proceeding.
- **Generated and ignored artifacts:** Do not add build output or cache (`target/`, `node_modules/`, `dist/`, coverage) or paths in `.gitignore` unless the user **explicitly** asks to track them.
- **Submodule:** Do not `git add` paths under `nebular-os/*` except bumping the submodule pointer (gitlink); see `nebular-os-vendor.mdc`.

## Hooks

- **Do not** bypass Git hooks with `--no-verify` / `-n` unless the user **explicitly** asks to skip hooks for that commit. Hooks (lefthook) enforce `cargo fmt`, clippy, eslint, type-check, and secret scanning.

